#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:9
msgid ""
"Decide how to preview slides in pull requests and deploy the deck from "
"main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:11
msgid "Context and Problem Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:13
msgid ""
"[ADR-0001](0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md) selected "
"Slidev for the PyCon JP 2026 talk deck. The deck entry point will be "
"`slides/slides.md`, and `slidev build` produces a static SPA that can be "
"deployed as a static site. We need two deployment flows: (1) a **per-PR "
"preview** so reviewers can visually verify slide changes during the PR "
"review process (issues [#294](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-"
"wasm/issues/294)–[#316](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-"
"wasm/issues/316)), and (2) a **main-branch deployment** so a live deck "
"URL is available from `main` without manual local builds. The repository "
"already deploys a redirect page to the `gh-pages` branch via [`deploy-"
"redirect.yml`](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-"
"wasm/blob/main/.github/workflows/deploy-redirect.yml) (using `peaceiris"
"/actions-gh-pages`), pointing to Read the Docs. The decision must be "
"compatible with or replace this existing deployment. Which hosting "
"platform and CI workflow strategy should we adopt for both per-PR slide "
"previews and main-branch deck deployment?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:15
msgid "Decision Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:17
msgid ""
"**Zero-cost hosting**: The project is an open-source, community-driven "
"effort; the hosting solution must be free for public repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:18
msgid ""
"**Automatic deployment on push to main**: The deck should update "
"automatically when slide source is merged to `main`, with no manual "
"deploy step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:19
msgid ""
"**Per-PR preview uniqueness**: Each pull request must get a unique, "
"stable preview URL that reflects its own branch state, so reviewers can "
"compare slides without building locally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:20
msgid ""
"**Ease of setup**: The solution should require minimal external accounts,"
" API tokens, or configuration beyond what is already in the repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:21
msgid ""
"**Maintenance burden**: Prefer a solution with few moving parts and well-"
"maintained dependencies, so the deployment pipeline does not become a "
"source of toil."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:22
msgid ""
"**Compatibility with the existing `gh-pages` redirect workflow**: The "
"existing `deploy-redirect.yml` pushes a redirect `index.html` to the `gh-"
"pages` branch (Pages source: \"Deploy from branch\"). The slide "
"deployment must coexist with or cleanly replace this workflow without "
"breaking the Read the Docs redirect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:24
msgid "Considered Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:26
msgid ""
"[GitHub Pages (Deploy from branch)](https://docs.github.com/en/pages"
"/getting-started-with-github-pages) + [rossjrw/pr-preview-"
"action](https://github.com/rossjrw/pr-preview-action) — Main deck "
"deployed to the `gh-pages` branch via `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages`; PR "
"previews deployed to `gh-pages/pr-preview/pr-N/` via `rossjrw/pr-preview-"
"action`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:27
msgid ""
"[GitHub Pages (GitHub Actions source)](https://docs.github.com/en/pages"
"/getting-started-with-github-pages/using-custom-workflows-with-github-"
"pages) + [`actions/upload-pages-artifact`](https://github.com/actions"
"/upload-pages-artifact) / [`actions/deploy-"
"pages`](https://github.com/actions/deploy-pages) — Main deck deployed via"
" the official Pages artifact pipeline; PR previews as downloadable build "
"artifacts (no live URL)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:28
msgid ""
"[Netlify](https://www.netlify.com/) — Main deck deployed to Netlify on "
"push to main; PR previews via Netlify's automatic deploy previews"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:29
msgid ""
"[Vercel](https://vercel.com/) — Main deck deployed to Vercel on push to "
"main; PR previews via Vercel's automatic preview deployments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:30
msgid ""
"[Cloudflare Pages](https://pages.cloudflare.com/) — Main deck deployed to"
" Cloudflare Pages on push to main; PR previews via Cloudflare Pages "
"preview deployments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:31
msgid ""
"GitHub Actions build artifact only — No live deployment; build the deck "
"on PRs and upload as a GitHub Actions artifact that reviewers download "
"and serve locally"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:32
msgid ""
"[Read the Docs](https://readthedocs.org/) subpath — Deploy the slide deck"
" within the existing Read the Docs documentation site as a subpath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:34
msgid "Decision Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:36
msgid ""
"Chosen option: \"GitHub Pages (Deploy from branch) + rossjrw/pr-preview-"
"action\", because it is the only option that satisfies every decision "
"driver simultaneously — it is zero-cost, fully GitHub-native (no external"
" accounts or tokens), provides unique per-PR live preview URLs with "
"automatic cleanup, deploys automatically on push to main, and is fully "
"compatible with the existing `gh-pages` redirect workflow that already "
"uses `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages` on the `gh-pages` branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:38
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:40
msgid ""
"Good, because per-PR previews get unique, stable live URLs at "
"`https://<owner>.github.io/<repo>/pr-preview/pr-<N>/` with an automatic "
"PR comment containing the link, so reviewers can visually verify slide "
"changes without cloning or building locally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:41
msgid ""
"Good, because `rossjrw/pr-preview-action` automatically cleans up preview"
" deployments when a PR is closed, preventing the `gh-pages` branch from "
"accumulating stale preview directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:42
msgid ""
"Good, because the main deck deploys automatically on push to `main` at "
"`https://<owner>.github.io/<repo>/slides/`, giving a shareable live deck "
"URL with no manual step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:43
msgid ""
"Good, because both workflows use the same `gh-pages` branch with \"Deploy"
" from branch\" Pages source as the existing `deploy-redirect.yml`, so the"
" Read the Docs redirect at the root is preserved and the slide deck lives"
" at a `/slides/` subpath."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:44
msgid ""
"Good, because no external service accounts, API tokens, or credit cards "
"are required — everything runs through `GITHUB_TOKEN` and GitHub's free "
"Pages offering for public repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:45
msgid ""
"Bad, because the `deploy-redirect.yml` workflow must be updated to set "
"`keep_files: true` (or add `clean-exclude: pr-preview/`) so its current "
"`keep_files: false` does not delete PR preview directories and the "
"`slides/` directory on every redirect deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:46
msgid ""
"Bad, because Slidev must be built with the correct `--base` path "
"(`/pyvista-wasm/slides/` for main, `/pyvista-wasm/pr-preview/pr-<N>/` for"
" previews) so that asset URLs resolve correctly under the subpath "
"deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:47
msgid ""
"Neutral, because `rossjrw/pr-preview-action` does not support PRs from "
"forks (the action notes this as a v2 roadmap item), so external "
"contributors' PRs would not get automatic previews — acceptable for this "
"project where slide PRs (#294–#316) are expected from the maintainer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:49
msgid "Confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:51
msgid "Compliance with this decision will be confirmed by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:53
msgid ""
"A `deploy-slides.yml` workflow exists in `.github/workflows/` that builds"
" the Slidev deck with `slidev build --base /pyvista-wasm/slides/` on push"
" to `main` (when `slides/**` changes) and deploys to the `gh-pages` "
"branch under a `slides/` subdirectory via `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages` "
"with `keep_files: true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:54
msgid ""
"A `preview-slides.yml` workflow exists in `.github/workflows/` that "
"builds the Slidev deck on `pull_request` events (opened, synchronize, "
"reopened, closed) when `slides/**` changes, and deploys via `rossjrw/pr-"
"preview-action` to `gh-pages/pr-preview/pr-<N>/`, posting a comment on "
"the PR with the preview URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:55
msgid ""
"The existing `deploy-redirect.yml` is updated to use `keep_files: true` "
"(or equivalent `clean-exclude`) so it no longer removes the `slides/` and"
" `pr-preview/` directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:56
msgid ""
"The main deck is accessible at `https://tkoyama010.github.io/pyvista-"
"wasm/slides/` after a push to `main`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:57
msgid ""
"A PR touching `slides/` receives a comment with a preview URL at "
"`https://tkoyama010.github.io/pyvista-wasm/pr-preview/pr-<N>/`, and the "
"preview directory is removed when the PR is closed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:59
msgid "Pros and Cons of the Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:61
msgid "GitHub Pages (Deploy from branch) + rossjrw/pr-preview-action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:63
msgid ""
"See [https://github.com/rossjrw/pr-preview-"
"action](https://github.com/rossjrw/pr-preview-action)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:65
msgid ""
"Good, because it is fully GitHub-native — no external accounts, API "
"tokens, or credit cards are needed; everything runs through "
"`GITHUB_TOKEN` and GitHub's free Pages offering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:66
msgid ""
"Good, because `rossjrw/pr-preview-action` deploys each PR to a unique "
"subpath (`pr-preview/pr-<N>/`) on the existing GitHub Pages site, posts a"
" comment with the preview URL on the PR, updates the preview on new "
"commits, and cleans up automatically when the PR is closed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:67
msgid ""
"Good, because it is compatible with the existing `deploy-redirect.yml` "
"workflow, which already uses `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages` to push to the "
"`gh-pages` branch with \"Deploy from branch\" Pages source — no Pages "
"source migration is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:68
msgid ""
"Good, because the main deck can be deployed to a `slides/` subpath on the"
" same `gh-pages` branch, preserving the root redirect to Read the Docs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:69
msgid ""
"Good, because Slidev's official hosting documentation provides a GitHub "
"Pages deploy example using `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages`, so this approach"
" is well-documented and battle-tested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:70
msgid ""
"Neutral, because `rossjrw/pr-preview-action` requires the repository's "
"Pages source to be \"Deploy from branch\" (not \"GitHub Actions\"), which"
" is already the case for this repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:71
msgid ""
"Bad, because the existing `deploy-redirect.yml` uses `keep_files: false`,"
" which would delete the `pr-preview/` and `slides/` directories — a one-"
"line change to `keep_files: true` is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:72
msgid ""
"Bad, because PRs from forks do not get automatic previews (a known "
"limitation of `rossjrw/pr-preview-action`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:74
msgid ""
"GitHub Pages (GitHub Actions source) + actions/upload-pages-artifact / "
"actions/deploy-pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:76
msgid ""
"See [https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages"
"/using-custom-workflows-with-github-"
"pages](https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages"
"/using-custom-workflows-with-github-pages)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:78
msgid ""
"Good, because it uses GitHub's first-party, officially maintained Pages "
"deployment actions (`actions/upload-pages-artifact` and `actions/deploy-"
"pages`), which are well-documented and actively maintained."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:79
msgid ""
"Good, because it is zero-cost and GitHub-native, requiring no external "
"accounts or tokens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:80
msgid ""
"Good, because Slidev's official hosting documentation includes a sample "
"workflow using `actions/upload-pages-artifact` + `actions/deploy-pages`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:81
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it requires switching the repository's Pages source from"
" \"Deploy from branch\" to \"GitHub Actions\", which means the existing "
"`deploy-redirect.yml` workflow (using `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages`) would"
" no longer work and must be replaced by incorporating the redirect page "
"into the Pages artifact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:82
msgid ""
"Bad, because `actions/deploy-pages` is restricted to the default branch "
"for the `github-pages` environment, so per-PR live preview URLs are not "
"natively supported — PR builds can only be uploaded as downloadable "
"artifacts, which reviewers must download and serve locally, failing the "
"per-PR-preview-uniqueness driver for a *live* URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:83
msgid ""
"Bad, because migrating the Pages source breaks the existing redirect "
"workflow and adds migration complexity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md
#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:85
msgid "Netlify"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:87
msgid ""
"See [https://www.netlify.com/](https://www.netlify.com/) and [Slidev "
"Netlify hosting](https://sli.dev/guide/hosting.html#netlify)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:89
msgid ""
"Good, because Netlify automatically creates unique preview deployment "
"URLs for each PR with no extra workflow configuration, strongly "
"satisfying the per-PR-preview-uniqueness driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:90
msgid ""
"Good, because Netlify deploys on push to main automatically and provides "
"a free tier for public projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:91
msgid ""
"Good, because Slidev's official hosting documentation provides a "
"`netlify.toml` template for Netlify deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:92
msgid ""
"Good, because Netlify handles SPA routing (redirects to `index.html`) out"
" of the box, which Slidev's SPA build requires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:93
msgid ""
"Neutral, because the free tier has build-minute and bandwidth limits that"
" are generous but not unlimited."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:94
msgid ""
"Bad, because it requires creating a Netlify account, linking the "
"repository, and storing an API token as a repository secret — adding "
"external dependency and setup overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:95
msgid ""
"Bad, because it is not compatible with the existing `gh-pages` redirect "
"workflow; the redirect would need to be migrated or the deck would live "
"on a separate Netlify domain, splitting the project's web presence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md
#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:97
msgid "Vercel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:99
msgid ""
"See [https://vercel.com/](https://vercel.com/) and [Slidev Vercel "
"hosting](https://sli.dev/guide/hosting.html#vercel)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:101
msgid ""
"Good, because Vercel automatically creates unique preview deployment URLs"
" for each PR with no extra workflow configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:102
msgid ""
"Good, because Vercel deploys on push to main automatically and provides a"
" free tier for hobby projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:103
msgid ""
"Good, because Slidev's official hosting documentation provides a "
"`vercel.json` template for Vercel deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:104
msgid ""
"Neutral, because the free tier has usage limits and Vercel's commercial "
"focus may introduce future pricing pressure for open-source projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:105
msgid ""
"Bad, because it requires creating a Vercel account, linking the "
"repository, and storing an API token — adding external dependency and "
"setup overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:106
msgid ""
"Bad, because it is not compatible with the existing `gh-pages` redirect "
"workflow; the deck would live on a separate Vercel domain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md
#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:108
msgid "Cloudflare Pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:110
msgid "See [https://pages.cloudflare.com/](https://pages.cloudflare.com/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:112
msgid ""
"Good, because Cloudflare Pages provides automatic preview deployments for"
" each PR and deploys on push to main."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:113
msgid ""
"Good, because the free tier is generous with unlimited bandwidth and "
"build requests for public projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:114
msgid ""
"Neutral, because Slidev's official hosting documentation does not include"
" a Cloudflare Pages template, so the configuration must be written from "
"scratch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:115
msgid ""
"Bad, because it requires creating a Cloudflare account, linking the "
"repository, and storing an API token — adding external dependency and "
"setup overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:116
msgid ""
"Bad, because it is not compatible with the existing `gh-pages` redirect "
"workflow; the deck would live on a separate Cloudflare Pages domain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:118
msgid "GitHub Actions build artifact only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:120
msgid ""
"Good, because it requires no hosting platform at all — the built deck is "
"uploaded as a GitHub Actions artifact on PRs, and reviewers download and "
"serve it locally with `npx vite preview` or any static server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:121
msgid ""
"Good, because it is zero-cost and fully GitHub-native with no external "
"accounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:122
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it is trivial to set up: a single `actions/upload-"
"artifact` step after `slidev build`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:123
msgid ""
"Bad, because reviewers must download, extract, and serve the artifact "
"locally, which is friction-heavy and fails the per-PR-preview-uniqueness "
"driver for a *live* URL that can be shared with non-technical reviewers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:124
msgid ""
"Bad, because there is no automatic main-branch deployment — the deck is "
"not accessible at a live URL without manual artifact download, failing "
"the automatic-deployment driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md
#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:126
msgid "Read the Docs subpath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:128
msgid "See [https://readthedocs.org/](https://readthedocs.org/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:130
msgid ""
"Good, because the project already uses Read the Docs for documentation "
"(`pyvista-js.readthedocs.io`), so deploying the deck as a subpath would "
"keep all project web presence in one place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:131
msgid ""
"Good, because Read the Docs is free for open-source projects and deploys "
"automatically on push to main."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:132
msgid ""
"Neutral, because Read the Docs is designed for Sphinx/MkDocs "
"documentation, not arbitrary static SPAs — embedding a Slidev SPA would "
"require a custom build step or iframe embedding within an Sphinx page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:133
msgid ""
"Bad, because Slidev's SPA build is not a documentation site, so "
"integrating it into Read the Docs would be an awkward fit requiring "
"workarounds (e.g., committing the built `dist/` to the repo and serving "
"it as static files within the Sphinx build)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0002-decide-slide-preview-and-deployment-strategy.md:134
msgid ""
